  "cast": {
    "en": {
      "voice_id": "e8e5fffb-252c-436d-b842-8879b84445b6",
      "name": "Cathy",
      "why": "Cartesia 'Coworker: nice young adult female for casual conversations': someone talking at her desk, not an announcer. Chosen over Sabrina, Layla, Dorothy and Connie on register consistency across the day (audition groups consistency-L1/L2/L4, same settings per line). Every voice drops on the declarative L2, but Cathy keeps one register: median F0 264 / 217 / 241 Hz on L1 / L2 / L4, a 3.4-semitone range, against 6.8 st for Sabrina (266 / 180 / 221), 6.0 for Dorothy, 6.1 for Connie and 8.0 for Layla. That keeps her audibly the same woman from the inbox to the evening note. All her takes pass transcription and land on the storyboard timings."
    },
    "de": {
      "voice_id": "3f4ade23-6eb4-4279-ab05-6a144947c4d5",
      "name": "Karin",
      "why": "Native German ('Companion: friendly female for casual conversations'). Median F0 225-260 Hz sits inside Cathy's register (217-264 Hz), so it reads as the same woman switching language; relaxed effort and a warm, darker spectrum. Lea and Rena sit lower; Jennifer elided 'komme' to 'komm' (pasted text would not match); Cathy speaking German has a non-native accent."
    }
  },
